msgid "If fourth kans have been declared (not all by the same player), the game ends in an abortive draw."
msgstr ""

msgid "If multiple players win on the same tile, only the closest player in turn order gets the win."
msgstr ""

msgid "If one Fan always implies another Fan, only one of them can be scored."
msgstr ""

msgid "If one of your kongs is concealed, you are instead awarded Two Kongs (6 Fan). If both are concealed, you are instead awarded Two Concealed Kongs (8 Fan)."
msgstr ""

msgid "If someone calls fuun to upgrade a chon of winds, you may call ron on the added tile. Doing so awards chanfuun (1 han).)"
msgstr ""

msgid "If someone calls kan on your discard and wins off the kan draw, you are responsible for the full payment."
msgstr ""

msgid "If someone calls kan to upgrade an open triplet, and you are waiting to win on that tile, you may specially call ron on that added tile. Doing so awards the 1 han yaku Chankan."
msgstr ""

msgid "If someone kans your discard and tsumos off the replacement tile (rinshan), you pay the full amount."
msgstr ""

msgid "If someone's exposed melds indicate that they have no possible winning hand, you can press the skull button for that player to declare their hand dead. If the declaration is correct, then the target player can no longer draw or discard, and must sit out of the rest of the round. If the declaration is incorrect, you suffer that penalty instead."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the AI is stuck or missing, clicking the center compass will try to unstuck them."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the dealer (East wind) is tenpai at exhaustive draw, the round repeats. If honba is enabled, this adds one honba."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the dealer (East wind) wins, the round repeats."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the dealer loses (by discarding the winning tile, or by someone else self-drawing their winning tile) then the dealer pays an extra 1 Tai plus 2 Tai for each dealer continuation. The only way to avoid the dealer penalty while passing on the dealership is if someone else discards into another player's winning hand."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the dealer wins, or the round ends in a draw, the dealer remains dealer."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the first discard for all four players is the same wind tile, the round ends in an abortive draw."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the first discard for every non-dealer is the same as the dealer's first discard, the dealer must immediately pay 1 point to each player times challenge multipliers."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the game ends due to there being no more tiles in the wall, players in tenpai gain score based off their best wait."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the game results in a draw, the round repeats."
msgstr ""

msgid "If the round ends in a draw, the round repeats."
msgstr ""

msgid "If there are multiple winners, then the earliest winner in turn order gets the full payment for the hand, and the other winners get half each. As for riichi sticks, each winner first takes back their own riichi stick (if any) and any remaining non-winner riichi sticks are evenly divided among winners."
msgstr ""

msgid "If won by discard, the discarder pays %{discarder_pays}x and all nondiscarders pay %{nondiscarders_pay}x."
msgstr ""

msgid "If won by discard, the discarder pays %{discarder_pays}x."
msgstr ""

msgid "If won by discard, the discarder pays nothing and non-discarders pay %{nondiscarders_pay}x."
msgstr ""

msgid "If won by self-pick, all players pay %{self_pick_pay}x."
msgstr ""

msgid "If won by self-pick, there is no payment."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you achieve multiple limit scores, they stack instead of being capped at 10 Fan."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you are waiting for a tile to win, but one of your winning tiles is among your discards (including tiles called by other players), then you are 'in furiten' and cannot win by ron (including chankan). You can still win by tsumo."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you are waiting for a tile to win, but one of your winning tiles is among your discards (including tiles called by other players), then you cannot win if someone discards the same tile (but you can still win by self-draw). The difference from Riichi's furiten rule is that you can still win with non-discarded tiles that you are waiting for."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you can, you may discard into a ready hand by announcing Ting to lock your hand. If you win, you are awarded 1 Tai."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you can, you may discard into tenpai (ready hand) by declaring 'riichi' to lock your hand. If your discard passes, you bet %{bet} points. If you win, you are awarded Riichi (1 han yaku). If you declared riichi on your very first discard, then you are instead awarded double riichi (2 han). Calls before the riichi declaration invalidate double riichi."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you complete a set of four flowers (%{t1}, %{t2}, %{t3}, or %{t4}) after the initial flower declaration round, then you are immediately paid 50 from each player."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you deal the last dragon called for a daisangen hand, or the last wind called for a daisuushii hand, you are responsible for that single yakuman payment if they tsumo, or half of the yakuman payment if they ron off someone else."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you deal the last dragon called for a daisangen hand, or the last wind called for a daisuushii hand, you are responsible for the yakuman payment if they tsumo, or half of the payment if they ron off someone else."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you deal the last kan tile called for a suukantsu hand, you are responsible for the yakuman payment if they tsumo, or half the payment if they ron off someone else."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you deal the last tile called for kan for a suukantsu hand, you are responsible for that single yakuman payment if they tsumo, or half of the yakuman payment if they ron off someone else."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you discard a gold tile, you may only win by self-draw."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you discarded a tile called as someone's fourth call, you are liable for paying for their hand if they win."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you do not win any hands by the end of the game, you pay each player a penalty."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you end with an exhaustive draw, and no one has called any of your discards, and your discards are all terminal or honor tiles, a nagashi payment occurs, which is equivalent to a %{is} tsumo."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you had won by self-draw, everyone would pay you 12+8 points (plus one for 1 Fan Self-Drawn), totalling 63. It's worth a lot to self-draw!"
msgstr ""

msgid "If you have called Phỗng with a joker, and later you draw another copy of the same tile, you may 'bounce' the joker by substituting the joker for that drawn tile. The joker goes into your joker/flower pool as if replaced normally (scores points). You cannot bounce jokers when there are no more tiles remaining in the wall."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you have multiple win patterns, you add their fan values and receive a bonus fan for each."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you hover over your 9 bamboos, you can see that your wait is not only the 4 bamboo, but also any galaxy four! Let's discard a 9 bamboo."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you kan and then tsumo on the replacement tile, you are awarded rinshan (1 han)."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you reveal a set of four flowers (%{t1}, %{t2}, %{t3}, or %{t4}) at this stage, then you are immediately paid 100 from each player."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you scroll down now, or during a game, you can see the JSON representation of the ruleset you're playing. Which you can modify and play in the Custom ruleset."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you use no more than 3 jokers it becomes 25 Faan, and if you use no more than one joker it's 30 Faan."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you win by discard, everyone pays you the hand value but the discarder's payment is doubled. If you win by self-draw, all players pay double the hand value."
msgstr ""

msgid "If you win on a discard (like we just did) the discarder pays the 12 points, and on top of that, every player pays 8 points. This means an 8 Fan hand is worth 32 points at minimum."
msgstr ""

